    "notes": [
      "Six visual STLs from the locked user 10.15 STEP; source vertices already in metres. C4 adapter is the STEP part, not an independent CNC adapter asset.",
      "Masses 153/299/140/140/18/35 g use the approximate weighed integer column. Source SW COM and principal moments are converted without mass scaling.",
      "SW-to-mount coordinates are [SW_y,SW_x,-SW_z]; screenshots use cm and g*cm^2. Raw screenshots, principal axes, conversion and hashes are retained.",
      "Camera COM was corrected from the new user SW screenshot on 2026-10-23 and checked against locked STEP geometry. The active COM is [-0.02305604,0.00009135,0.06677412] m in taccap_camera_body_link; mass stays manually assigned 18 g and original SW principal moments are not scaled. Superseded COM=0 and the original erroneous screenshot are retained in provenance. Hardware mass distribution remains uncalibrated.",
      "Inherited semantic frames, limits, joint axes and mimic are locked to the 08.03 archive. No physical parameters copied from the archive.",
      "This separately versioned asset has two URDF entries and one simplified collision set. Existing xense.taccap_slave compatibility APIs and ROS retain the archive; current TacCap workcell recipes explicitly select this 10.15 asset. New MJCF/USD not generated.",
      "Camera-only handoff: physical camera_link.STL and 18 g belong to taccap_camera_body_link; inherited reference/optical/EEF nodes remain geometry-free and inertia-free. The initial geometry handoff supplied no new physics; the corrected user SW COM screenshot was supplied separately on 2026-10-23.",
      "Both URDFs expose the same nominal flange_link origin and axes. Bare root is virtual; mounted root carries C4 geometry and 35 g. Base is +12 mm along flange +Z. Dedicated-adapter assemblies compose this internal transform to preserve mounting seats. Legacy taccap_mount_link is only a locked source-frame name.",
      "2026-10-23: user-directed model version/path/ID migration from slave-v2026.10.15 and xense.taccap_slave_v2026_10_15. The current model release is v2026.10.23-rc.1; source.revision retains the actual 10.15 CAD revision. Raw geometry, measurements, frozen provenance and all physical/kinematic definitions are retained."
    ]
  },
